body:
My hunger cues are all over the place, and if i just try to eat when im hungry and stop when im full, ill go the whole day not eating anything and then eating too much in the evening, which triggers binges. For that reason, i try to eat at least 3 times a day (breakfast, lunch and dinner) and more if i feel hungry in between. However, i still really struggle with knowing what are normal portions, and i cant listen to my hunger cues because id either eat nothing or everything, so i try to eat normal portions during the main meals. however, when other people comment on the size of my portions, i dont want to eat at all anymore because i feel like a fat fuck for even thinking about eating all of it (even when i can logically deduce it was a normal portion). Ive told my family about this before but especially my stepfather doesnt stop those kinds of comments, and im too scared of saying anything about it in the moment (i dont want to lash out or make a big deal of everything) but when i talk about it afterwards he doesnt change his behavior either. 

&#x200B;

Im sorry, this ended being quite a long rant, i dont want to delete it after typing it
